# =============================================================================
# Dynamic API Validator — root .gitattributes                          (OBJ-024)
#
# LFS rules MUST be in place before the first 'git add'. A file staged without
# them is stored as an ordinary blob, and moving it to LFS afterwards requires
# rewriting history.
#
# ⚠️ repo.arconnet.com is self-hosted, so whether LFS is enabled server-side is
# UNVERIFIED from this workspace. If the first push rejects LFS objects, the
# fallback is to exclude these files rather than commit them as plain blobs.
# =============================================================================

# --- Git-LFS -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The three source PDFs: 78.64 MB, and incompressible (gzip 89-95%), so they
# would cost their full weight in every clone. Static vendor/reference documents
# that never diff usefully.
#   PAM Administrative Guide.pdf   40.15 MB
#   Client Manager Guide.pdf       26.26 MB
#   PAM API (Internal Team).pdf    12.23 MB  <- the payload reference
*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# 201.53 MB — the single largest file in the repository and the only one over
# GitLab's default 100 MB per-blob limit, so LFS is what makes it pushable at
# all. Note it is a *derived* artifact of the excluded pam/PAM product repo
# (its .graphify_root names 'pam\PAM'), and it is regenerable — exclusion was
# offered and declined, so it is tracked via LFS instead.
# OBJ-025: matched by '**/graphify-out/graph.json' rather than the literal path.
# A literal path stops matching the instant artifacts/graph/ moves, and git then stores
# 201 MB as an ordinary blob -- silent at commit, rejected at push, and fixable
# only by rewriting history. This form also covers dev-scope and any future scope.
**/graphify-out/graph.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- Binary: never diff, never line-ending-normalise -------------------------
*.xlsx binary
*.xls  binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary

# --- Text: keep line endings exactly as committed ----------------------------
# No '* text=auto'. This tree holds Windows PowerShell scripts that must stay
# CRLF (the *_register_*.ps1 task registrars are documented as 7-bit ASCII and
# encoding-sensitive) alongside POSIX shell and Python. Normalising the whole
# tree on a Windows checkout would rewrite thousands of files on first commit
# and bury the real content in whitespace churn.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
